Deterministic reference/Pangolin N-ablation atlas (GRCh38 / GENCODE v50). N
masking measures cis-sequence sensitivity, NOT physical ASO occupancy or PSI.
Each of four tissue usage channels is reported separately, averaged over its
three released models, matching feng.titration.gpu_scores' channel selection.
All public coordinates are 1-based inclusive. FaiFastaReader converts at I/O;
mask slices convert in footprint_mask. Minus-strand input is reverse-
complemented once; readout indices then follow transcript orientation. CLI:
--smoke --output-dir DIR, or --config JSON --output-dir DIR. JSON:
{"assembly":"GRCh38", "annotation":"GENCODE v50", "windows":[ {"locus":"id",
"chrom":"chr5", "strand":"+", "center":70076574, "distance":50,
"sites":[{"position":70076574,"kind":"donor"}]}],
"grid":{"lengths":[18],"start":70076584,"end":70076601,"stride":1}} Sites and
grid must be prespecified independently of measured outcomes. One absolute
genomic tiling interval per config; use separate configs for distant loci. No
inferred or outcome-selected splice sites are added by this engine.

